WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:02.130
- [Interviewer] All right Baby.

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:02.963
- Yes.

00:00:02.963 --> 00:00:03.960
- Baby welcome back.

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:04.793
- Hey.

00:00:06.054 --> 00:00:07.120
- So you had the baby.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:11.330
- I did on Friday the 13th, November 13th.

00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:12.630
- Tell me how that went.

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:14.000
- It was really crazy.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.623
I had her in a tent on Gladys.

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:19.210
It all happened so fast I don't know.

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:21.460
I was in labor like the whole night.

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:22.660
- You had the baby in the tent?

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:23.493
- Yeah

00:00:23.493 --> 00:00:24.326
By myself.

00:00:24.326 --> 00:00:26.590
I cut her umbilical cord
and all that by myself.

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:29.253
I zip tied her umbilical cord and cut it.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:33.200
It was really crazy.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.350
Somebody called the ambulance.

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:37.480
And they made me go to the hospital after.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:39.330
But she was fine.

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:41.793
Yeah, I named her Zahra Miracle.

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:45.650
I don't know she's...

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:48.713
It was a blessing.

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:50.868
- And where is she now?

00:00:50.868 --> 00:00:53.950
- Right now she's
currently in a foster care,

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:56.570
because they want me to
take some parenting classes.

00:00:56.570 --> 00:00:58.513
And some other classes,

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:00.273
I don't know.

00:01:00.273 --> 00:01:02.283
But I'm in a program doing that.

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:06.203
- Did they test you for drugs?

00:01:06.203 --> 00:01:09.363
- Yeah, she only had weed in her system.

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:13.680
Remember I was doing
meth in the beginning.

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:15.310
And then I found out.

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:16.191
You know what I'm saying?

00:01:16.191 --> 00:01:19.683
I stopped really doing meth at the end.

00:01:21.704 --> 00:01:24.770
I didn't want her to have
nothing in her system.

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:26.984
So she had weed in her system.

00:01:26.984 --> 00:01:27.817
But they took her because...

00:01:27.817 --> 00:01:29.930
I guess because I had
her in tent on Gladys.

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:34.240
- Yeah that can't be the
best place to have a child.

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:35.180
- Right.

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:39.160
Well I couldn't really help it.

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:40.513
It was all so fast.

00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:43.760
- So it's been like three weeks now?

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:45.200
- It's been about a month.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:46.323
Friday the 13th.

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:48.750
- And you must be missing her.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:49.583
Right?

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:51.673
- Yeah.

00:01:51.673 --> 00:01:52.506
- It's gotta be hard.

00:01:52.506 --> 00:01:53.690
- Yeah it is.

00:01:53.690 --> 00:01:54.523
It's crazy.

00:01:54.523 --> 00:01:55.453
She looked just like me.

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:59.960
- Is there a chance that she
might go to another family?

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:05.180
- She's in a foster care but until,

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:08.020
they put me into a more intensive program.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:09.950
They're saying all I get right now,

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:12.893
is six hours visitation supervised a week.

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:18.090
So they wanna put me in a more intensive,

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:20.230
inpatient program where you can't leave.

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:21.470
'Cause at this program I'm at,

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:23.470
you could just leave and go as you want.

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:27.980
- So you're still living on the street?

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:29.590
- No I'm in a program.

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:34.030
Yeah I'm in a program
at the Colorado Hotel.

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:35.670
It's basically like a little hotel room.

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:36.723
You got a roommate.

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:42.430
But it's like a big ass
fun drug house for kids.

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:44.020
Like you can do whatever
the fuck you want.

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:46.820
You can leave for 72 hours
without them putting you out.

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:50.643
You come back once every
72 hours to check in.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:54.370
- Looking forward,

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:55.440
what do you think the chances are,

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:58.293
of you doing everything that's
necessary to keep the baby?

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.010
- Well I'm waiting on them to find me,

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:05.560
another more intensive program.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:08.000
But it's on their term and their call.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.870
I can't already try to
look for programs and shit.

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:11.703
And they was like,

00:03:11.703 --> 00:03:12.893
yeah we're gonna find one,

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:17.330
that's best suited for you or whatever.

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:18.580
So it's all on their term.

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:19.413
I don't know.

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:22.533
I'm hoping that they'll get,

00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:27.120
that shit done and contact
me back and get me moved.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:30.060
But I don't know.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:31.450
'Cause they haven't contacted me yet,

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:32.723
and it's been two weeks.

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:36.260
- Do you see your baby every day?

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:38.450
- No I haven't seen her yet.

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:40.810
They haven't contacted me back to see her.

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:41.810
To schedule no appointment.

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:42.830
They just called me and told me,

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:46.680
that I'm approved for six hours
supervised visitation a week

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:48.270
- Six hours a week?

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:49.103
Okay.

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:56.200
And going through this stress,

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:59.463
is it difficult for you not to use?

00:04:03.429 --> 00:04:06.610
- It is more hard now not to use,

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:08.270
than it was when I was pregnant with her.

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:10.863
Because I don't have her with me.

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:13.830
They're talking about
whenever they move me,

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:15.850
and they get me into the program.

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:17.520
The more intense the program,

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:19.840
that I'll be able to get her,

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:21.460
and have there in my custody all the time.

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:22.490
You know what I'm saying?

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:25.080
So I'll be able to have
her in the program with me.

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:26.233
That's what I wanted.

00:04:27.744 --> 00:04:31.040
But right now it's a lot harder.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:32.840
It's a lot harder for me not to use.

00:04:35.390 --> 00:04:37.440
I used the day I got out of the hospital.

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:40.900
Leaving her at the hospital.

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:43.100
The first thing I went
and did was get high.

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:46.210
- And then if you don't get her back,

00:04:46.210 --> 00:04:47.810
you're much more likely
to start using again.

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:48.643
Right?

00:04:48.643 --> 00:04:49.476
- Right.

00:04:49.476 --> 00:04:51.300
If I didn't get her back.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:54.553
Probably would be strung
the fuck out here.

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:03.460
- Alright Baby your story is hard.

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:04.920
It's (chuckles) hard for me to hear.

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:06.890
- Yeah it's really hard.

00:05:06.890 --> 00:05:07.790
- I feel bad for your baby.

00:05:07.790 --> 00:05:08.863
I feel bad for you.

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:17.140
- Yeah. I just hope that
(snuffling) I'll get her back.

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:23.310
- Can your family help in any way?

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:24.933
- No they won't help me.

00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:30.286
- They won't help you?

00:05:30.286 --> 00:05:31.490
- (snuffles) Thank you.

00:05:31.490 --> 00:05:32.323
- What do you mean they won't help you?

00:05:32.323 --> 00:05:34.800
- They won't do shit for me.

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:36.480
I can't even call them to talk to...

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:38.693
My little sister I call
and talk to her but,

00:05:40.850 --> 00:05:42.890
she's always working or in school.

00:05:42.890 --> 00:05:44.433
She takes care of my daughter.

00:05:49.648 --> 00:05:50.481
Oh no.

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:53.683
Oh fuck.

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:57.330
- Wish I could just transplant
you to another city.

00:05:57.330 --> 00:05:58.180
- Yeah.

00:05:58.180 --> 00:05:59.650
- Far from Skid Row.

00:05:59.650 --> 00:06:02.665
- Man I hate this place.

00:06:02.665 --> 00:06:04.998
(snuffling)

00:06:05.890 --> 00:06:10.533
But I'm just hoping everything
will work out for the best.

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:12.473
At the end.

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:15.653
They say God does everything for a reason.

00:06:18.082 --> 00:06:20.520
- If there was ever a reason to get clean,

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:22.197
this would be it.

00:06:22.197 --> 00:06:23.030
- That's what I said.

00:06:23.030 --> 00:06:25.023
That's why I think I've been,

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:28.510
strong minded about it now.

00:06:28.510 --> 00:06:31.763
I've been able to do it as much as I have.

00:06:36.903 --> 00:06:37.736
- Alright baby.

00:06:37.736 --> 00:06:38.920
Thank you so much for
giving us the update,

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:41.620
and I wish you all the luck in the world.

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:42.580
- Thank you.

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:43.890
- You'll get your baby back.

00:06:43.890 --> 00:06:44.723
- Thank you.

00:06:44.723 --> 00:06:45.556
- And get outta here.

00:06:47.030 --> 00:06:47.863
- Hell yeah.

00:06:47.863 --> 00:06:49.460
As soon as I get her back I'll be gone.

00:06:50.926 --> 00:06:53.004
(snuffling)

00:06:53.004 --> 00:06:54.004
- Thank you.

